      "writtenOn": "2022-07-01T02:37:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, yeah, that is indeed not great. Maybe the best thing to do is to add a completely separate construction mechanism, just for tests (that doesn\u0027t involve any static initialization magic). I am not a java expert, this may be worth running by someone like Remi or Lorenzo.\n\n--\n\nOne additional point, static initialization in tests is usually bad, especially if it can fail / throw. Failures in static / class initializers aren\u0027t reported correctly, so they are not immediately obvious in the logs. This isn\u0027t directly an issue here, I don\u0027t think, but just something to keep in mind.",
